Worked for 28s

Now the Java side is finally using the correct mode:

KrbAuthType=2

and the previous JAAS/KDC timeout is gone. The remaining GSS initiate failed is now in the ticket-cache/service-principal stage. Cloudera documents that KrbAuthType=2 uses the Kerberos ticket cache via KRB5_CONFIG and KRB5CCNAME. 

The first thing I would fix is that in your last command you ran only:

java -jar ImpalaStressTesting-1.0-SNAPSHOT-jar-all.jar

but your earlier KRB5_CONFIG=... was scoped only to the kinit command. Export both variables before Java:

export KRB5_CONFIG=/home/rise37432/ImpalaStressTest/securityConfigs/kerb5.ini
export KRB5CCNAME=FILE:/tmp/krb5cc_206621

echo $KRB5_CONFIG
echo $KRB5CCNAME

klist

Then request the exact service ticket Java needs for the LB:

kvno impala/master-vm-cdp01-uat-app-387066.hodomain.local@TESTHODOMAIN.LOCAL

Then check:

klist

You want to see both:

krbtgt/TESTHODOMAIN.LOCAL@TESTHODOMAIN.LOCAL

and:

impala/master-vm-cdp01-uat-app-387066.hodomain.local@TESTHODOMAIN.LOCAL

Then run:

java \
-Djava.security.krb5.conf="$KRB5_CONFIG" \
-Dsun.security.krb5.debug=true \
-jar ImpalaStressTesting-1.0-SNAPSHOT-jar-all.jar

The kvno result is the key discriminator:

- If kvno says something like Server not found in Kerberos database, then the LB SPN is missing. The required SPN is:
  impala/master-vm-cdp01-uat-app-387066.hodomain.local@TESTHODOMAIN.LOCAL
- If kvno succeeds but Java still gives GSS initiate failed, then the likely problem is on the Impala side: the backend impalad keytabs do not contain the LB principal. Cloudera says the Impala Daemons Load Balancer setting should be configured as LB_HOST:PORT; with Kerberos enabled, Cloudera Manager adds impala/LB_HOST@REALM to all Impala daemon keytabs, followed by an Impala restart. 

For your environment that setting should correspond to:

master-vm-cdp01-uat-app-387066.hodomain.local:21050

So run these exact commands next:

export KRB5_CONFIG=/home/rise37432/ImpalaStressTest/securityConfigs/kerb5.ini
export KRB5CCNAME=FILE:/tmp/krb5cc_206621

klist

kvno impala/master-vm-cdp01-uat-app-387066.hodomain.local@TESTHODOMAIN.LOCAL

klist

The output of kvno will tell us whether this is still client-side or definitively an LB/Impala SPN configuration issue.
